<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore restores refinery run on Feb 21.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore restores refinery run on Feb 21.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore has restored runs at its refinery to full capacity of 59,000 tonnes per day (435,000 barrels per day) on February 21, a company spokeswoman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The refinery at Pulau Bukom, off southern Singapore, reduced crude throughput by 4,000 tonnes per day since January 17.  </p>
<p>&quot;We always said that we will be monitoring the market,&quot; the spokeswoman said. &quot;We are moving in response to market conditions and we moved back up in line with improved conditions.&quot;</p>
<p>Shell had cut its refining runs due to weak refining margins.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
